From: SORABBYNGO Engineering <kernel@sorabbyngo.com>
Subject: [PATCH 5/9] mm/slab: guard page insertion — OpenBSD malloc hardening

OpenBSD's malloc(3) inserts guard pages randomly between allocations to
detect heap overflows. This patch brings the concept to kernel slab:

  1. CONFIG_SORABBYNGO_SLAB_GUARD: adds an unmapped guard page after
     every N-th slab allocation (N=64 default, tunable via sysctl).
     Overflows into the guard page trigger an immediate BUG().

  2. Slab freelist randomisation: on kmalloc, the freelist order within
     each slab is shuffled using get_random_u32(). This mirrors
     OpenBSD's malloc chunk randomisation.

  3. Use-after-free detection: freed slab chunks are poisoned with
     0xDF (OpenBSD uses 0xDF for freed memory, 0xCD for uninitialised).

These changes increase memory pressure slightly but provide meaningful
protection against heap spray attacks — relevant for Cyberwall and
CML's sandboxed external call path.
---
 mm/slub.c                         |  48 +++++++++++++
 include/linux/sorabbyngo_slab.h   |  18 +++++
 lib/Kconfig.sorabbyngo            |  14 ++++
 3 files changed, 80 insertions(+)

diff --git a/mm/slub.c b/mm/slub.c
--- a/mm/slub.c
+++ b/mm/slub.c
@@ -1,5 +1,6 @@
 #include <linux/slab.h>
 #include <linux/random.h>
+#include <linux/sorabbyngo_slab.h>
 
+#ifdef CONFIG_SORABBYNGO_SLAB_GUARD
+/*
+ * sorabbyngo_slab_poison - poison freed chunks (OpenBSD 0xDF pattern)
+ * Called from kmem_cache_free() before returning chunk to freelist.
+ */
+void sorabbyngo_slab_poison(void *obj, size_t size)
+{
+	memset(obj, SORABBYNGO_SLAB_FREE_POISON, size);
+}
+
+/*
+ * sorabbyngo_slab_check_poison - verify free-poison on alloc
+ * Any byte that isn't 0xDF indicates a use-after-free write.
+ */
+void sorabbyngo_slab_check_poison(const void *obj, size_t size)
+{
+	const u8 *p = obj;
+	size_t i;
+
+	for (i = 0; i < size; i++) {
+		if (p[i] != SORABBYNGO_SLAB_FREE_POISON) {
+			pr_emerg("sorabbyngo: use-after-free detected at "
+				 "%p+%zu (byte 0x%02x, expected 0x%02x)\n",
+				 obj, i, p[i], SORABBYNGO_SLAB_FREE_POISON);
+			BUG();
+		}
+	}
+}
+#endif /* CONFIG_SORABBYNGO_SLAB_GUARD */
